DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The mmttrraaccee() function installs hook functions for the memory‐allocation
       functions  (mmaalllloocc(3),  rreeaalllloocc(3)  mmeemmaalliiggnn(3),  ffrreeee(3)).  These hook
       functions record tracing information about memory allocation and  deal‐
       location.  The tracing information can be used to discover memory leaks
       and attempts to free nonallocated memory in a program.

       The  mmuunnttrraaccee()  function  disables  the  hook  functions  installed by
       mmttrraaccee(), so that tracing information is no  longer  recorded  for  the
       memory‐allocation  functions.   If  no hook functions were successfully
       installed by mmttrraaccee(), mmuunnttrraaccee() does nothing.

       When mmttrraaccee() is called, it checks the value of the  environment  vari‐
       able MMAALLLLOOCC__TTRRAACCEE, which should contain the pathname of a file in which
       the tracing information is to be recorded.  If the pathname is success‐
       fully opened, it is truncated to zero length.

       If  MMAALLLLOOCC__TTRRAACCEE is not set, or the pathname it specifies is invalid or
       not writable, then no hook functions are installed, and mmttrraaccee() has no
       effect.  In set‐user‐ID and set‐group‐ID programs, MMAALLLLOOCC__TTRRAACCEE is  ig‐
       nored, and mmttrraaccee() has no effect.

